   "rate": 0.88,
   "at": 0.6
  },
  {
   "id": "vo2",
   "role": "voice",
   "src": "voice/vo2.wav",
   "text": "A [[router]]router picks the spike. It reads every spike's description and the case together, in one [[seq]]sequence. At about [[full]]fifty-six spikes the descriptions fill it, and the case has no room left.",
   "speaker": "bm_fable,bm_fable,bm_lewis",
   "rate": 0.88,
   "at": "vo1.out+0.5"
  },
  {
   "id": "vo3",
   "role": "voice",
   "src": "voice/vo3.wav",
   "text": "So make it a [[tree]]tree. A router's options can be spikes, or other routers, and each router reads only its own children. [[dim]]Dim the lights goes to [[voice]]voice, then [[home]]smart home, then [[lights]]lights, then [[leaf]]dim. Three short reads instead of one long one.",
   "speaker": "bm_fable,bm_fable,bm_lewis",
   "rate": 0.88,
   "at": "vo2.out+0.5"
  },
  {
   "id": "vo4",
   "role": "voice",
   "src": "voice/vo4.wav",
   "text": "No router ever reads the whole list, so the library can keep [[grow]]growing. Broad spikes split into narrow ones: voice commands become fifty-four separate intents. The ball fills in, and gets [[round]]rounder.",
   "speaker": "bm_fable,bm_fable,bm_lewis",
   "rate": 0.88,
   "at": "vo3.out+0.5"
  },
  {
   "id": "vo5",
   "role": "voice",
   "src": "voice/vo5.wav",
   "text": "On sixty-two leaves, the tree [[acc]]routes within about a point of one flat router, reading fewer tokens. And a [[new]]new spike, given only its description, finds its cases more often, because it competes only with its siblings.",
   "speaker": "bm_fable,bm_fable,bm_lewis",
   "rate": 0.88,
   "at": "vo4.out+0.5"
  },
  {
   "id": "vo6",
